\section*{Appendix}
\begin{proof}[Proof of Lemma~\ref{sysdecombip}]
Since $K$ is even, by a result of Auerbach and Laskar~\cite{auerbach} the complete bipartite graph with  vertex classes $\{A_1, \dots, A_K \}$ and $\{B_1, \dots, B_K \}$ has a Hamilton decomposition.
(a$_1$) follows by orienting the edges of each of these Hamilton cycles to obtain directed Hamilton cycles $C_{1}, \dots, C_{K/2}$.

For each $i_1,i_2,i_3,i_4 \le K$, we partition $\mathcal J_{i_1,i_2,i_3,i_4}$ into $K/2$ sets $\mathcal J_{j,i_1,i_2,i_3,i_4}$ (one for each $j\le K/2$)
whose sizes are as equal as possible.
Therefore, (a$_2$) follows by setting $\mathcal{J}_{j} := \bigcup_{\I \le K} \mathcal{J}_{j , \I}$.
Note that, for each $i_1,i_2,i_3,i_4 \le K$ and $j \leq K/2$,
\begin{align*}
|\mathcal J_{j, \I}| & \le  \frac{ 2 |\mathcal J_{\I}|}{K}+1  \overset{{\rm (c)}}{=}  \frac{2|\mathcal J|}{K^5}+1  \overset{{\rm (b)}}{\le} \frac{(1/2 - 2\mu - 2\rho) n}{K^5} +1 \\ 
& \le  (1-4 \mu - 3 \rho) m/K^4
\end{align*}
as $2K m  \ge (1- \eps_0)  n $ and $1 /n \ll \eps_0 \ll 1/K \ll \rho$.

