Rejected at Step 0. The proposed inverse-generated decompositions pass G and V but fail H:

- Track A: the paper provides no hardness result for the planted distribution and instead uses flow, matching, and cycle-merging constructions in its dense regimes.
- Track B: hidden random factors have no public compact route; visible Walecki structure takes the same 253 output operations mechanically and compactly at the largest fitting instance.

The full analysis, theorem regimes, output-cap calculation, and measured Walecki cost are in [REJECTED.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1401.4178/REJECTED.md). This follows the instruction to stop before building or running oracles when Step 0 fails H. The relevant definitions and results were checked against the [full arXiv paper](https://arxiv.org/pdf/1401.4178).
